 ## Background
-This method is part of the FastGS (Fast Gaussian Splatting) optimization pipeline, which aims to accelerate and improve the training of 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1, unofficial]. It leverages multi-view consistency as a more robust signal for densification than single-view gradients, addressing the issue of overfitting to specific viewpoints or noise.
+The method originates from the FastGS repository, which provides an unofficial implementation of optimized Gaussian Splatting training routines [S1, unofficial]. It leverages multi-view consistency as a more robust signal for densification than single-view gradients, addressing the issue of overfitting to specific viewpoints or noise [S1, unofficial].
 
